  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1200 PM CDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nWednesday through Sunday:\n\nContinue to see a trend in the global models of the upper-level\nlow and trough beginning to track eastward into Quebec midweek \nand onward. As a result it will shift the active pattern \neastward as well. While cannot completely rule out a stalled \nboundary and some shower/storm activity across the area \nWednesday as hints of a mid- level vorticity lobe swings down \nthe backside of the gradually departing upper-level trough, but \nany activity will be highly dependent on the prior days \nactivity. However by Thursday, surface high pressure begins to \nbuild into the Upper Midwest and continue to build through \nFriday as the upper-level ridge axis builds across the central \nCONUS. This will bring a drier pattern to southern WI through \nthe end of the week. \n\nThen the long range models and ensembles trends turn more \nactive into the weekend as a series of mid-level shortwave \ntrough as projected to swing across the region. This will bring \na periodic shower and thunderstorm chances across the area \nSaturday and Sunday. \n \nTemps in the extended trend toward normal through the middle of\nthe week before dipping to near or even below normal temps \ntoward the end of the week. \n\nWagner",
